Z||000000||Matthew_Fiero||08-27-2001||11:18 PM||||The turn signals on my 85 GT blinks VERY slow<BR>do you know what causes this? and how to fix it<BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||08-28-2001||07:54 AM||||Are you sure that all the bulbs are lighting?  Current draw causes the blinker to heat up enough to cycle.  If a bulb is burned out the current draw is low (often too low to allow the blinker relay to cycle).<P>Have you ever noticed that when you plug in a trailer wiring harness to a tow car the blinkers cycle much faster?  That's because of the increased current demand due to the trailer light bulbs.<P>Take a look to see that all bulbs are lighting up.  Compare side to side and you may find a bulb on one side that is not working.||||reg||1
